{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773767003,"nonce":"3YZVZsei0jDhP1cb/wzKkE8aldk=","title":"Treat clean agent exit (result:success) as @@DONE@@","message":"When the agent finishes work and exits cleanly with result.subtype=success, but forgets to output @@DONE@@, nightshift marks the session as suspended:unexpected. This is wrong — a clean success exit IS done.\n\n## Current behavior\n\n1. Agent completes work, outputs 'implementation is complete' in plain text\n2. Agent exits with result type=result, subtype=success\n3. Stream parser emits PROCESS_EXIT event\n4. SessionRunner event loop breaks, status is still 'working'\n5. post_run_action hits the catch-all: suspended:unexpected\n6. Session is stuck, requires manual resume\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nWhen the agent exits with result.subtype=success:\n- Treat it as equivalent to @@DONE@@\n- Commit WIP, set status to done:pending-review\n- Proceed to pre-review rebase and review as normal\n\n## Implementation options\n\nA. Stream parser (adapters/agents/claude_code.py): detect result event with subtype=success, emit a synthetic MarkerType.DONE event before PROCESS_EXIT\nB. Session runner (core/session.py): after event loop ends, if status is still 'working' and agent exited cleanly (check exit code or result), trigger the done path\nC. post_run.py: in the 'working' status branch, check if the agent exited cleanly before treating as max-turns\n\nOption A is cleanest — the stream parser already parses these events.\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- adapters/agents/claude_code.py: detect result.subtype=success, yield DONE-equivalent event\n- tests/test_stream_parser.py: test that success result triggers done path\n\nREQ-002, REQ-015","files":null}]}